## Problem (tree truth)

Wave-1 closed the **wrong** 2.9 question (“does bare `println(SECRET)` refuse?”).
Peer 2 + Security named the real hole: a SECRET IDENT that appears **after an
inner `RPAREN` still inside the sink args**. Live product host (07:49 ELF)
confirms it. Fairy re-proved 2026-08-12 (`/tmp/s29b_ideas_probes`, virgin cwd):

| Shape (`// SECRET: tok`) | check | emit-c | emit-llvm | Class |
|--------------------------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|
| `println(tok)` bare | **BLOCK** | **BLOCK** | (front-door) | wave-1 floor — keep |
| `println("tok")` lit | ALLOW | ALLOW | ALLOW | 0 FP — keep |
| `println(("x") + tok)` grouping then `+` | **FN** OK | **FN leak** `oo_print_str(oo_str_concat((oo_str_lit("x")), tok))` | **FN** rc=0, `c"s3cret"` in module | **this hole** |
| `eprintln(("x") + tok)` same | **FN** OK | **BLOCK** (C-text guard) | **FN** (no guard) | check/llvm hole; emit-c saved by eprintln rail |
| `println(id(1), tok)` later top-level after call | **FN** OK | **BLOCK** (2nd-arg rescan) | **FN** first-arg only | check/llvm hole |
| `println(f(g(), tok))` nested call, secret after inner `)` | **FN** OK | **FN leak** `oo_print_str(f(g(), tok))` | (same front-door) | **this hole** |
| Official `s29_println_guard_smoke.sh` | exit 0 | exit 0 | — | **bare only** — not this class |

| Fact | Evidence |
|------|----------|
