**Two FN subclasses (do not collapse):**

| ID | Shape | Why FN | Who still BLOCK |
|----|-------|--------|-----------------|
| **H-later** | `println(id(1), tok)` / `println((n), tok)` | Check walker’s first `)` ends the **whole** arg list. Later SECRET never seen | stmt emit-c (outer loop + `c_emit_expr_c` then next arg) |
| **H-same** | `println(("x") + tok)` / `println(f(g(), tok))` | Check **and** stmt inner scan stop at grouping/call `)`. `c_emit_expr_c` then lowers the **full** expr and **prints `tok`** | eprintln emit-c only (C-text) |

Wave-1 smoke covers neither. Domain A “hole class empty” is H-later/H-same **untested**, not absent.

**Not this wave:** full IFC, `${}` (5.8), 2.10 wrappers, product `print` API, emit-bc front-door (Security R2 — name, do not bury), log-family check list (wave-1 I6).

## Constraints (hard)

1. **Path A only** — named-sink refuse of SECRET IDENT in println/eprintln args, not “perfect taint.”
2. **Ship-now is depth-aware IDENT walk.** Not fake C `args`. User + Memory H3 + wave-1 I5 already killed the other architecture.
3. **Do not greenwash wave-1 I1 / Domain A ALREADY_FIXED** onto this class. Bare dual refuse **stays**. RPAREN class is **open**.
4. **LLVM has no emit_guard.** Check-path depth **is** the llvm/wasm fix. Deleting the front-door is an FN.
5. **Stmt `println` is not a C call.** Joining per-arg C texts for `c_secret_emit_guard` is a **second re-lexer** + concat (`args = args + ", " + a`). Memory forbids it as the 2.9 land.
6. **`c_secret_emit_guard` takes C arg texts**, not toks. Check calling it is still the stale DE2.9 sentence (wave-1 I9).
7. **Both rails.** Check-only depth leaves H-same emit-c leak. Stmt-only depth leaves check/llvm/wasm H-later/H-same FN.
8. **Reuse the existing depth machine.** Prefer `c_secret_scan_call` (WT already depth) over a third walker. `count_paren_args` is the oracle, not a secret helper.
9. **Smoke CWD must be cache-clean** (s71 R9). Extend `s29_println_guard_smoke.sh` — do not invent a second 2.9 truth.
10. **Line pressure** — no new monofile. `c_emit_print.oo` **87**. `c_emit_secret.oo` WT **219** / HEAD **259**.
11. **Fairy writes ideas only** — DE owns land + prove. Do not mix 2.9 close with 7.10/2.10 claims on the same hunk.

## Darwin scorecard (path-A residual)

Axes 0–10 (higher = survives compile cycle). Sum/5 ≈ rank:

| Axis | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Close** | Moves 2.9 wave-2 (H-later + H-same refuse on check + emit-c + llvm) |
| **Honest** | Named residual; no “walker now calls emit_guard”; no wave-1 ALREADY_FIXED lie |
| **Smoke** | Cheap: grouping+`+`, later-arg after call, nested `f(g(), tok)`, string no-FP, bare still BLOCK |
| **Entropy** | Lowers \(S\) (untested RPAREN, WT depth unproved, DE2.9 / I5 theater) |
| **Ship** | ≤ depth on existing IDENT walk + smoke; no fake `args`, no builtin delete |

**Rule:** losers pruned. 1–2 winners advance to DE this sprint turn.

